MF= 2 Resonance parameters                                        9861 1451   47
  MT=151                                                          9861 1451   48
  Resolved resonance parameters (MLBW: 1.0e-5 - 1.0 keV)          9861 1451   49
    (same as JENDL-3.3)                                           9861 1451   50
    Resonance parameters were taken from Moore et al./5/ by       9861 1451   51
    assuming an average radiative capture width of 0.035 eV and   9861 1451   52
    fission width of 0.035 eV. Two hypothetical resonances at     9861 1451   53
    1.4 and -3.5 EV were adopted to reproduce the 2200-m/s        9861 1451   54
    cross sections and resonance integrals/6,7/. Scattering       9861 1451   55
    radius of 9.23 fm was estimated from the shape elastic        9861 1451   56
    scattering cross section calculated with CASTHY/8/.           9861 1451   57
                                                                  9861 1451   58
  Unresolved resonance parameters (1 - 150 keV)                   9861 1451   59
    Parameters (URP) were determined with ASREP code/9/ so as to  9861 1451   60
    reproduce the cross sections in this energy region. URP are   9861 1451   61
    used only for self-shielding calculations.                    9861 1451   62
