                                                                  9861 1451  200
  Models and parameters used in the CCONE/10/ calculation         9861 1451  201
  1) Coupled channel optical model                                9861 1451  202
     Levels in the rotational band were included. Optical model   9861 1451  203
     potential and coupled levels are shown in Table 1.           9861 1451  204
                                                                  9861 1451  205
  2) Two-component exciton model/16/                              9861 1451  206
    * Global parametrization of Koning-Duijvestijn/17/            9861 1451  207
      was used.                                                   9861 1451  208
    * Gamma emission channel/18/ was added to simulate direct     9861 1451  209
      and semi-direct capture reaction.                           9861 1451  210
                                                                  9861 1451  211
  3) Hauser-Feshbach statistical model                            9861 1451  212
    * Moldauer width fluctuation correction/19/ was included.     9861 1451  213
    * Neutron, gamma and fission decay channel were included.     9861 1451  214
    * Transmission coefficients of neutrons were taken from       9861 1451  215
      coupled channel calculation in Table 1.                     9861 1451  216
    * The level scheme of the target is shown in Table 2.         9861 1451  217
    * Level density formula of constant temperature and Fermi-gas 9861 1451  218
      model were used with shell energy correction and collective 9861 1451  219
      enhancement factor. Parameters are shown in Table 3.        9861 1451  220
    * Fission channel:                                            9861 1451  221
      Double humped fission barriers were assumed.                9861 1451  222
      Fission barrier penetrabilities were calculated with        9861 1451  223
      Hill-Wheler formula/20/. Fission barrier parameters were    9861 1451  224
      shown in Table 4. Transition state model was used and       9861 1451  225
      continuum levels are assumed above the saddles. The level   9861 1451  226
      density parameters for inner and outer saddles are shown in 9861 1451  227
      Tables 5 and 6, respectively.                               9861 1451  228
    * Gamma-ray strength function of Kopecky et al/21/,/22/       9861 1451  229
      was used. The prameters are shown in Table 7.               9861 1451  230
